      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRICK AND STICK (2) struggled to get involved last start after settling off pace at this track, but prior to that won by 2.75 lengths at this track (17.06) beating FRYING BONNIE in a Mix 2/3 on July 17. Goes very well from this draw with three wins and three minor placings from seven starts. Can make amends. BOBBY BONUS (3) was safely held in tougher company last start after settling well back at Grafton, but prior to that won easily by 4 lengths at this track (17.19) beating CHAMPAGNE TALKS in a Mix 3/4 on July 27. Good beginner aided by a nice draw. Can figure in the finish. CHAMPAGNE TALKS (6) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing seventh (20.92) last time in a Grade 5 at Grafton. Has good early speed and can overcome the tricky draw. Likely to be thereabouts. FRYING BONNIE (7) has strong credentials from this draw.",
